Frame pacing metrics: percentiles, jitter, stutter ratio, the longest run of slow frames, and who was busy
inside each spike

`[gow-frame]` printed a mean and four thresholds. A hitch report needs the shape of the distribution, not its centre.
`FrameWindow::analyze()` now returns p50/p95/p99/p99.9, max, jitter (standard deviation of the stored intervals), the
count and ratio of frames above 1.5 x p50, the count of frames above max(2 x p50, 100 ms), the longest run of
consecutive frames above 2 x p50, and over_200/over_300. The work runs once per report window on a copy of the stored
intervals; `add()` only gained the two counters, so the per-frame path is unchanged.

`recordGuestFrame()` also differences `ps2_perf`'s exclusive per-thread buckets between two frame entries, so every
frame above the fan-out threshold (max(2 x the previous window's p50, 100 ms)) prints
`[gow-frame-spike] t=.. ms=.. ee=.. vu=.. gs=.. iop=.. gwait=.. upload=.. hwait=..`. The threshold uses the previous
window's p50, so the attribution adds no second pass. `attr=on|off` in the window line says whether those buckets are
being charged at all (they are only when GOW_PERF_DIAG is set).

Measured, ship deck, Asia disc, 0.5x, Intel HD Graphics 4400, 70 s, GOW_PERF_DIAG=1 GOW_FRAME_DIAG=1. Cold start
reports as its own window: t=6.569, 2 frames, max 4000.06 ms, and that frame is ee 311.5 / iop 190.1 / guest_wait
3498.3 / host_wait 3874.1 ms (a load stall, not a frame). Steady state, t=46.7..66.8 s, 80..89 frames per window:
p50 52.1..59.6 ms, p95 76.6..119.0 ms, p99 130.8..169.2 ms, p99.9 130.8..169.2 ms, jitter 14.3..24.9 ms, stutter
4.5..11.2 %, 1..5 spikes, longest run 1..4, over_200=over_300=0. Every steady-state spike is VU1-attributed:
t=52.392 ms=169.21 vu=159.6 gs=87.4 ee=78.2; t=57.396 ms=156.37 vu=152.4 gs=23.2 ee=52.3; t=65.060 ms=127.31
vu=121.5 gs=36.9. `[gs-gpu]` in the same run measures 4.6..11.7 ms per presented frame, and vu_ms is 4597..4685 of
each 5000 ms window, so the frame interval is the VU1 thread's time, not the chip's. This patch only measures: mean
frame rate is unchanged (guest_flip_hz 16.6..18.4 -> 14.8..18.4, scene drift; p50/p95 within the +/-10 % run band).

